# Rust build artifacts
/target
/dist

# Deployment config & secrets — ONLY the *.example templates are tracked.
#   deploy/bb-auth.env : the externalized, deployment-specific config (Cognito
#                        pool/client, service & login URLs, install paths). The
#                        real BB_AUTH_HMAC_KEY is generated on the host and lives
#                        only there — never in git.
#   deploy/access.json  : the real access file (emails + API key hashes). Only
#                        deploy/access.example.json is tracked.
#   deploy/settings.json: a real settings file, if one is ever kept here. Only
#                        deploy/settings.example.json is tracked. The live one is
#                        state on the host, like the access file.
*.env
/deploy/access.json
/deploy/settings.json

# Agent tool state, which is per-machine and never the repository's business. It holds
# whatever the operator has approved, and on this checkout that has included a live `bbk_`
# bearer inside a permission entry: it was covered only by the machine's own global
# excludes, which is a property of that machine and not of the next clone.
/.claude/

# Browser E2E suite (e2e/) — installed deps and per-run artifacts, never tracked
/e2e/node_modules
/e2e/artifacts

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
